SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"I've done my best, says Prayut","publisher":"Bangkok Post","publication_date":"2022-03-31","url":"https://www.bangkokpost.com/thailand/politics/2287730/ive-done-my-best-says-prayut","claim":"Prayut said he had tried his best, would respect voters' choice, was acting for the benefit of most people, and described the government's work as responding to unprecedented crisis and hardship.","locator":"lines 204-225","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct contemporaneous interview with attributed quotations.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Target-year public program statement.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Prayut's own public framing of his governing purpose.","contrary_evidence":["This is self-description, not independent proof of delivery."],"lenses":["8B.1","8B.9","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Thai parliament passes $93 billion budget bill at first reading","publisher":"The Fiji Times / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-06-03","url":"https://www.fijitimes.com.fj/thai-parliament-passes-93-billion-budget-bill-at-first-reading/","claim":"Thailand's parliament passed the first reading of the 3.185 trillion baht budget bill, and Prayut said it would support economic recovery after the crisis and help restore strong and sustained growth.","locator":"lines 99-106","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire story with exact budget figures and an attributed quote from Prayut.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct target-period budget action.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Prayut as prime minister and the cabinet-backed budget process.","contrary_evidence":["The first reading shows intent and mobilization, not full implementation or final outcomes."],"lenses":["8B.1","8B.2","8B.6","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"House approves delayed budget","publisher":"Bangkok Post","publication_date":"2022-08-25","url":"https://www.bangkokpost.com/thailand/politics/2376413/house-approves-delayed-budget","claim":"The House approved the 3.18-trillion-baht fiscal 2023 budget, which the government said would revive the economy and accelerate its economic master plan and other economic and social development plans.","locator":"lines 212-217","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous report on a completed budget approval with clear summary of intended use.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Target-year implementation milestone.","ruler_attribution":"Attributable to Prayut's government because it concerns the budgetary tool he led through parliament.","contrary_evidence":["Passing a budget does not itself prove effective execution on the ground."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.3","8B.6","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Thailand approves tax breaks for EVs, high potential foreigners","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-02-22","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/economy/thailand-approves-tax-breaks-for-evs-high-potential-foreigners-2769072","claim":"Thailand's cabinet approved tax incentives for electric vehicles and skilled foreigners, including lower import duty and excise tax on EVs and a goal of making 30 percent of auto production EVs by 2030.","locator":"lines 405-418","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting with specific policy measures, targets, and quoted ministerial justification.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct target-period policy action.","ruler_attribution":"Attributable to Prayut's cabinet and the economic policy line it controlled.","contrary_evidence":["The plan is a policy input; the source does not by itself show long-run success."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.3","8B.4","8B.6","8B.7"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Thailand approves tax cut on diesel to ease high prices","publisher":"Reuters via MarketScreener","publication_date":"2022-02-15","url":"https://www.marketscreener.com/news/latest/Thailand-approves-tax-cut-on-diesel-to-ease-high-prices-39472315/","claim":"The cabinet extended and enlarged the diesel excise-tax cut to 5 baht per litre for two months, and Prayut said the measure was necessary to protect people and manufacturing from higher living costs.","locator":"article body and quoted remarks","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters report with direct attribution and concrete policy terms.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct target-year crisis response.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Prayut as cabinet leader managing the fuel-price response.","contrary_evidence":["This is crisis management, not a durable structural reform."],"lenses":["8B.6","8B.8","8B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Thailand targets 5 million to 15 million foreign tourists this year","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-05-06","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/economy/thailand-targets-5-million-to-15-million-foreign-tourists-this-year-2819202","claim":"Thailand aimed for 5 million to 15 million foreign tourist arrivals in 2022 as it eased travel restrictions to support the tourism sector.","locator":"article body","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire report with a clear policy objective and sector-specific implementation context.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Target-year economic reopening policy.","ruler_attribution":"Attributable to Prayut's government because it concerns easing restrictions and sector revival policy.","contrary_evidence":["The article reflects a recovery push, but not whether the target was met."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.6","8B.7","8B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Thailand 2022 Investment Pledges up 39% to USD20 Billion Helped by FDI flows in Electronics, EV, Data Centers","publisher":"Thailand Board of Investment / PRNewswire","publication_date":"2023-01-13","url":"https://www.prnewswire.co.uk/news-releases/thailand-2022-investment-pledges-up-39-to-usd20-billion-helped-by-fdi-flows-in-electronics-ev-data-centers-301721247.html","claim":"Applications for investment promotion in 2022 reached 664.6 billion baht, up 39 percent, and a board meeting chaired by Prime Minister Prayut approved coordination for regional headquarters, renewable energy facilitation, and three large projects.","locator":"press release body","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official BOI release with quantitative results and explicit PM-chaired approvals.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Retrospective 2022 result announced in January 2023.","ruler_attribution":"Strongly attributable to Prayut's government and its investment-promotion machinery, though not solely to Prayut personally.","contrary_evidence":["The release shows a strong year for some sectors, but it does not exclude weaknesses elsewhere or establish durability."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.3","8B.4","8B.6","8B.7","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Thailand sees 22% drop in investment pledges this year","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-09-12","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/economy/thailand-sees-22-drop-in-investment-pledges-this-year-2890250","claim":"Thailand expected overall investment applications to fall 22 percent to 500 billion baht in 2022 after a first-half slump, while foreign investment more than halved year on year.","locator":"article body","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters report with specific year-on-year figures and policy response context.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Target-year outcome and adaptation evidence.","ruler_attribution":"Attributable to the Prayut government only in a limited sense because the figures also reflect global and sectoral conditions.","contrary_evidence":["The same report notes government measures to attract investors later in the year, so the final annual picture was mixed."],"lenses":["8B.7","8B.8","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Prayut puts Bhumjaithai in its place with House dissolution threat","publisher":"Nation Thailand","publication_date":"2022-02-15","url":"https://www.nationthailand.com/in-focus/40012361","claim":"Prayut used the threat of dissolving the House to warn coalition partner Bhumjaithai to toe the line, and he said he might have to dissolve the House if options ran out.","locator":"lines 19-27","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Thai reporting with direct attribution and coalition context.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Target-year coalition management.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Prayut's use of bargaining leverage over coalition partners.","contrary_evidence":["This shows leverage and discipline, but it is also a sign of coalition strain."],"lenses":["8B.3","8B.5","8B.9"]}
